Table~\ref{tab:dev} lists the best development configuration of every family. Among the @OG_N@ distinct configurations the frozen fixed mean ranked @OG_FRANK@th on the development fitness (@OG_FF@; optimum @OG_OPT@). With @OG_BUDGET@ evaluations, random search found a configuration in the top 5\% in @OG_RN5@ of the runs, the GaaR strategies in @OG_G5@ (greedy), @OG_R5@ (restart) and @OG_P5@ (population), and in the top 1\% in @OG_RN1@ against @OG_G1@, @OG_R1@ and @OG_P1@: GaaR was not better than random search here, because many configurations of the similarity-weighted family are nearly equivalent. The champions of the restart strategy and of random search were the same configuration (similarity-weighted, window 3, persistence 0.5; $F=$ @F_GAAR@), no better than the untuned rule. An earlier search of the scoring configuration itself (smoothing, axes, PCA dimension, rarity scale; 360 configurations; repository) gave a gain on fresh scenarios of @OLD_DIFF@ with a 95\% interval of @OLD_CI@, which includes zero.

